      "id": "M4113-A",
      "prompt": "A. A fictional industrial classifier produces three learned responses at each latent-feature position. A softmax over the three responses supplies input-dependent weights, and their weighted sum feeds the classifier. The draft says: 'A calibrated uncertainty module fuses formal belief masses by Dempster's rule and yields reliable class probabilities.' Only classification comparisons and a weighting ablation are available. Give two connected English overview sentences that retain the implemented operation, followed by a brief Chinese explanation of what can and cannot be claimed.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Describe feature-response weighting followed by diagnostic classification.",
        "Separate actual evidence from calibration or formal evidence-combination claims."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Call normalized latent weights calibrated class probabilities or invent Dempster combination.",
        "Replace the implemented classifier with an uncertainty/rejection architecture."
      ],
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "outcome": "pass",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4113-revised.md",
