    {
      "id": "M4113-B",
      "prompt": "B. A fictional paper defines C>=2 nonnegative classifier logits z=ReLU(h), E(z)=-log(sum_c exp(z_c)), and rejects a test sample as unknown when -E(z)<-5. Its algorithm updates parameters only on training batches, then computes test labels without updates. Nearby prose mentions a 'testing loss'. The author asks whether to copy this published-style rule and claim test-time adaptation. Explain the exact concern and minimal handoff in Chinese. Do not invent the intended correction or execute an experiment.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Check score range and inequality mathematically.",
        "Distinguish stated training/test operations from a nearby loss label; request bounded implementation clarification."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Certify the impossible rejection condition or silently replace its sign/threshold.",
        "Assert test-label optimization merely from testing-loss wording."
      ],
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "outcome": "pass",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4113-revised.md",
