      "prompt": "D. A fictional author-proposed classifier outputs nonnegative evidence e_k, defines alpha_k=e_k+1, S=sum_k alpha_k, predicted probabilities alpha_k/S, and uncertainty u=K/S. It rejects inputs with u above a threshold selected without final test labels. Held-out evaluation includes known and unknown fault classes, with known-class performance and unknown-rejection results but no probability-calibration analysis. Give two English sentences connecting the model outputs to its diagnostic decisions, and briefly advise in Chinese how to frame its contribution and evidence. Do not suppress its genuine uncertainty output or add numerical results.",
